<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nongsa jikseol</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1429</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Straight Talk on Farming</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Nongsa jikseol ('Straight Talk on Farming') is a Korean farming manual compiled in 1429 by order of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sejong-the-great">King Sejong</a>. Officials gathered the methods of experienced farmers in each province so that agriculture could follow Korean soils and climate rather than Chinese handbooks. It covered seeds, soil preparation and the cultivation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/millet">millet</a>, beans and other crops, and it was distributed to local officials to raise harvests.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nongsa-jikseol.jpg" alt="Nongsa jikseol" width="320" height="340" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 정초(鄭招), 변효문(卞孝文) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E8%BE%B2%E4%BA%8B%E7%9B%B4%E8%AA%AA_%EB%86%8D%EC%82%AC%EC%A7%81%EC%84%A4.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
